**Level ★★**

This program works, but it is hard to read:

```python
if age >= 13:
    if ticket == "yes":
        if banned == "no":
            print("Come in!")
        else:
            print("Sorry, you can't come in.")
    else:
        print("Sorry, you can't come in.")
else:
    print("Sorry, you can't come in.")
```

Write a version that does **exactly the same thing**, using **one** `if` with one condition, and one `else`.
